{"tool_name":"deploid","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"deploid","version":"0.5","home":"http://deploid.readthedocs.io/en/latest/index.html","license":"GPLv3","summary":"A software that deconvolutes mixed genomes with unknown proportions.","identifiers":["biotools:DEploid","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btx530"],"license_file":"COPYING","build":{"number":5},"requirements":{"build":["make","automake","autoconf",null,null],"host":["cppunit","zlib"],"run":["zlib"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/mcveanlab/DEploid/archive/v0.5-release.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["dEploid 2>&1 | grep \"dEploid\""]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"deploid","identifiers":["biotools:DEploid","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btx530"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"A software that deconvolutes mixed genomes with unknown proportions.","home_url":"https://github.com/DEploid-dev/DEploid","keywords":["Coinfection","Haplotypes","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Malaria, Falciparum","Plasmodium falciparum","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Sequencing","Genotype and phenotype","Genomics","Statistics and probability"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"deploid","home":"https://github.com/mcveanlab/DEploid","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Deconvolution of multiple infections in Plasmodium falciparum from high throughput sequencing data .","addition_date":"2018-06-18T18:07:36Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:42:17.471235Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:deploid","credit":[{"email":"gil.mcvean@bdi.ox.ac.uk","name":"Gil McVean","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"joe.zhu@bdi.ox.ac.uk","name":"Sha Joe Zhu","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://deploid.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Deconvolution","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3629"}]}],"name":"DEploid","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"d.gabrielaitis","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btx530","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: The presence of multiple infecting strains of the malarial parasite Plasmodium falciparum affects key phenotypic traits, including drug resistance and risk of severe disease. Advances in protocols and sequencing technology have made it possible to obtain high-coverage genomewide sequencing data from blood samples and blood spots taken in the field. However, analyzing and interpreting such data is challenging because of the high rate of multiple infections present. Results: We have developed a statistical method and implementation for deconvolving multiple genome sequences present in an individual with mixed infections. The software package DEploid uses haplotype structure within a reference panel of clonal isolates as a prior for haplotypes present in a given sample. It estimates the number of strains, their relative proportions and the haplotypes presented in a sample, allowing researchers to study multiple infection in malaria with an unprecedented level of detail.","authors":[{"name":"Almagro-Garcia J."},{"name":"McVean G."},{"name":"Zhu S.J."}],"citationCount":48,"date":"2018-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Deconvolution of multiple infections in Plasmodium falciparum from high throughput sequencing data"},"pmcid":"PMC5870807","pmid":"28961721"}],"topic":[{"term":"Genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0622"},{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"},{"term":"Statistics and probability","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2269"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"DEploid","home":"https://bio.tools/deploid","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Deconvolution of multiple infections in Plasmodium falciparum from high throughput sequencing data .","